  "name": null,
  "problem": "Select the correct options in the truth table below and use this to determine whether $¬(X⇒Y)∧¬(Y⇒X)$ is a contradiction.\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(X⇒Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬(Y⇒X)\\,$ | $\\,¬(X⇒Y)∧¬(Y⇒X)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nAccording to the table, $¬(X⇒Y)∧¬(Y⇒X)$ \n{{field-5}}\nalways false. Therefore, it \n{{field-6}} \na contradiction.",
